WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.200
When Smallville ended in 2011, it felt like
we were all ready to move on to bigger things.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.900
Superman and all his friends had once again
become big-screen heroes, and the CW was gearing

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.969
up for a new age of superhero shows like Arrow,
The Flash, and Legends of Tomorrow.

00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:19.930
Even the cast of Smallville seemed poised
for bulletproof careers outside the borders

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.810
of their little town in Kansas.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:26.699
Now that the hit show's been off the air for
more than half a decade — yes, really — let's

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:31.029
take a look at where some of the biggest stars
of Smallville are now.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:32.700
Tom Welling

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.880
For a few years, it seemed like Smallville
was going to be the start of a long acting

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.270
career for its lead, Tom Welling.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.470
Playing Smallville's Clark Kent was Welling's
first major role, but he soon secured parts

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:48.670
in the Steve Martin comedy Cheaper by the
Dozen and the 2005 horror remake The Fog.

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.530
And then … crickets.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.240
For the next six years, Tom Welling only appeared
in Smallville.

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.390
And since the show went off the air, he's
only appeared in three films — Parkland

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:06.030
in 2013, Draft Day in 2014, and The Choice
in 2016 — all of which received mixed reviews

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:10.030
and did nothing to reboot Welling's declining
status as an actor.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:15.000
Here's hoping Welling's career gets a second
wind so he can take flight once again.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.170
Allison Mack

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:21.800
Long before playing journalist Chloe Sullivan
in Smallville, Allison Mack was a common fixture

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:22.910
on TV.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:28.260
She's had steady work on both television shows
and TV movies since 1989, and after the end

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.620
of Smallville, Mack took a recurring role
in the FX show Wilfred and American Odyssey.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:37.890
So, she's certainly been busy, but even so,
the actress has also found time for off-screen

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.500
projects, like her singing career.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.530
Kristin Kreuk

00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:47.050
After years of playing Lana Lang on Smallville,
Kristin Kreuk decided to take leave of the

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:50.780
show in 2009 because she felt there was more
she could be doing.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:54.830
The actress was 19 when she first appeared
in the role, and when she left the show seven

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:58.370
years later, it was still pretty much her
only major part.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:02.140
Unfortunately, the decision might not have
been as wise as she hoped, because she went

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.240
on to star in the box office bomb Street Fighter:
The Legend of Chun-Li.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.700
From there, she surfed through a handful of
low-key roles before finally returning to

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:14.090
CW with a recurring arc in Beauty and the
Beast.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.310
Michael Rosenbaum

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:20.280
There's no doubt that Michael Rosenbaum gave
the character of Lex Luthor just the right

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.010
amount of charm and likability to contrast
the darkness within.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.250
“This is Smallville!

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:32.290
Meteor freaks, alien ships, cryptic symbols...these
threats are real.”

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:36.370
Perhaps the reason he was such a good match
for the DC universe is that he'd been a part

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:39.260
of it before and stuck around afterward, too.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.400
He'd also done voice work for the animated
series Batman Beyond and during Smallville's

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.620
run he went on to voice the Flash in the animated
Justice League series.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.950
Overall, Rosenbaum's career has been marked
more by voice acting than physical acting,

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:56.290
so while you might not see him as much anymore,
keep those ears peeled, because he's still

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.569
as busy as ever.

00:02:58.569 --> 00:02:59.569
John Glover

00:02:59.569 --> 00:03:05.110
Lionel Luthor, Lex's dad, was the main baddie
in the earlier seasons of Smallville, a role

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.300
perfectly fitting for John Glover.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:11.739
Although he's often tried to avoid being typecast
as a villain, he just seems to keep getting

00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:13.500
tossed in those roles.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:18.969
After all, he was the slimy advertising guy
in Robocop 2, the evil Jason Woodrue in Batman

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:23.290
&amp; Robin … and even the devil himself in
1998's Brimstone.

00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:27.700
On top of that, he's voiced the Riddler in
a long run of animated DC shows.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:30.400
Hey, when you've got it, you've got it.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.110
Erica Durance

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:37.030
Smallville took its sweet time to bring Lois
Lane into the fold, but in Season 4, actress

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:41.069
Erica Durance finally introduced the street-smart
reporter to the show.

00:03:41.069 --> 00:03:45.780
Like her on-screen persona, Durance fit the
bill of being smart, capable, and "slightly

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:46.780
neurotic."

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:50.569
Outside of Smallville, though, the Canadian
actress hasn't had the best of luck.

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:54.980
She's mostly appeared in a string of B-movies
like the video game flop House of the Dead

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.470
and the completely ignored Butterfly Effect
2, along with a smattering of small roles

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:04.980
in various TV shows, including a long-lasting
turn in the CTV medical drama Saving Hope,

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:09.670
so she's still showing the same sort of gumption
that made her right for Lois.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:12.080
Annette O'Toole

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.000
Smallville marked the second time that Annette
O'Toole fell into the world of Clark Kent,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.120
the first being her stint as Lana Lang in
1983's Superman III, which means that in the

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.629
course of her career she's played both Clark
Kent's girlfriend and his mom.

00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:29.370
“I suppose I have to face it: I’m not
gonna find what I want in Smallville anymore.”

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:35.060
She left Smallville after the sixth season,
but returned in 2010 for two more cameo episodes,

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:40.080
before returning to small roles in other shows,
TV movies, and stage plays.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.080
John Schneider

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:46.379
The actor portraying Jonathan Kent, Clark's
dad, was a busy working actor long before

00:04:46.379 --> 00:04:47.949
he ventured into Smallville.

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:52.759
He most famously played Bo Duke, one half
of the duo on the original Dukes of Hazzard

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:56.060
and had a long-running role on Dr. Quinn,
Medicine Woman.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:59.919
His post-Smallville career has been just as
prolific.

00:04:59.919 --> 00:05:01.490
Justin Hartley

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:06.349
Before Oliver "Green Arrow" Queen got his
own show, the hooded hero regularly appeared

00:05:06.349 --> 00:05:07.469
on Smallville.

00:05:07.469 --> 00:05:11.800
In this version, Queen was portrayed by Justin
Hartley, who, like much of the younger cast

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.599
of the show, counted this as his first big
role.

00:05:14.599 --> 00:05:18.949
Prior to getting cast as Oliver Queen, though,
Justin Hartley was actually slated to star

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:24.249
in an Aquaman series on the CW, and even filmed
the pilot before the show was dropped.

00:05:24.249 --> 00:05:29.039
Judging by the trailer, it's probably a good
thing the network decided to pass on Aquaman.

00:05:29.039 --> 00:05:33.699
Because sometimes, the world just isn't ready
for a bleach-blond surfer who fights crime.

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:40.120
Hartley has since returned to the TV spotlight
as Kevin on NBC's hit dramedy This Is Us.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:42.119
Cassidy Freeman

00:05:42.119 --> 00:05:46.909
As Tess Mercer in Smallville, Cassidy Freeman
got to venture into some very weird territory

00:05:46.909 --> 00:05:50.440
as the CEO of LuthorCorp who's actually Lex's
sister.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:55.009
It was an unforgettable twist, to be sure,
and that tends to be the case whenever Freeman

00:05:55.009 --> 00:06:00.460
takes on even a small role, like her turns
as Jack in Once Upon A Time and a 400-year-old

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.909
bloodsucker in The Vampire Diaries.

00:06:02.909 --> 00:06:07.180
Since Smallville wrapped, Freeman found new
work on Longmire.

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:08.680
Aaron Ashmore

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:13.690
This former child star — and identical twin
to Shawn of X-Men fame — became a series

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:18.460
regular as Jimmy Olsen, the Daily Planet photographer
who was engaged to Chloe.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:23.009
Never a household name, Aaron Ashmore nevertheless
mustered enough star power to take the lead

00:06:23.009 --> 00:06:29.490
role in a handful of low-budget horror movies,
like 2009's Fear Island and 2010's The Shrine,

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:33.599
before joining the main cast for Syfy's well-received
show Killjoys.

00:06:33.599 --> 00:06:37.319
He might still be a little jealous of his
look-alike sibling, though, because at least

00:06:37.319 --> 00:06:39.319
he got to play with some sci-fi powers.

00:06:39.319 --> 00:06:41.349
But what are ya gonna do?

00:06:41.349 --> 00:06:42.860
Thanks for watching!

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:45.949
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:45.949 --> 00:06:48.649
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

